This directory contains code and text adapted from paseo-supervision
(https://github.com/hoangnb24/paseo-supervision), source commit
1bad19b8ee6c58482494f56a3d8c6edb4f969ee1.

The upstream Work is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0); a copy is at the upstream
repository root (LICENSE). Upstream carries no NOTICE file; the copyright
holder line in its LICENSE is unfilled, so attribution here names the
project and commit.

Adapted portions:

- assessment.ts — the rubric question text (rubric 2, extended in rubric 3
  with SLP-original turn-scoped closure wording) (guard, leadBrief,
  peerHandback, leadHandling instructions and criteria) reuses and edits
  wording from upstream server/jev.ts `questions`; the strict Choice answer
  handling (strict Zod schemas, unique-maximum probability distributions,
  ~1-sum validation, confidence threshold, conservative unknown) is adapted
  from the same file. The no_action_required choice, the code-offered link
  questions, per-axis gates and independent-finding judgment are original
  to this repository.
- observer.ts — serialized queue/generation mechanics and the
  refresh-before-send / mark-before-send / no-retry delivery shape adapted
  from upstream server/observer.ts. The client-bootstrap supervisor sync
  RPC is not ported.
- delivery.ts — the alert's framing (suspected communication issue, review
  required, not artifact acceptance, route repair through the Lead, the
  originating Peer is not the only valid recipient of handling, quoted
  evidence is untrusted) paraphrases the upstream alert prompt; the
  persisted attempt store, per-finding dedupe, deferral and bounded
  excerpts are original.
- capture.ts — the correlation idea (latest user_message boundary,
  confirmed-send evidence) and the recognized send names/JSON-string input
  follow upstream server/communication.ts; per-family send extraction is
  original to this repository.
- ../../client/supervision-controls.ts — the recipient-workspace bell follows
  upstream index.client.tsx; it calls this repository's server-side CAS
  writer instead of host settings. The upstream Command Center actions are
  not carried (the Human chose Manager-card pickers instead).

Modified relative to upstream: provider-aware extraction for the SLP family
registry, SLP role routing and discovery defaults, report-route semantics,
Jev capability gating, daemon-home binding, schema migration, bounded
metadata-only persistence, and per-axis findings instead of an all-axis
veto. See docs/spec/supervision-integration.md for the divergence contract.
